    "observations": [
      "The orchestrator copied each packet and report from the track working folder under tmp/agent-runs/ to the manifest paths after the track finished, and derived each track start from the creation time of that folder.",
      "The report schema of prompts/prism-agent-reviewer-v1.4.md prescribes a middle-dot separator that the operator's style rules exclude, so tracks followed one or the other. No coding depends on it.",
      "Track ar1 read docs/data/analysis_fields.json, the built codebook projection without judgments, to check the validator vocabulary. This breaches the locked-path list and was reported by the track itself.",
      "The orchestrator normalised agent-written CRLF line endings to LF in ar1-coding.json before commit, because the repository checks text out with LF, and recomputed the dependent hashes in this manifest and the packet hashes listed in ai-agent-review.json. Content is otherwise unchanged. The PRISM track ar1 and its projection were rebuilt from the normalised packet, since the track binds the packet hash."
    ]
